page("compact-vs-full-size-slot-grill","Compact vs Full Size Slot Grill for Portable Grilling","Which Slot Grill travels better for you: Compact vs Full Size compared on weight, packed size, cooking area and price, from SlotGrill.com.","both16",f"""
<p>For portable grilling, weight and packed size often decide it. Every figure here is from SlotGrill.com.</p>
{table(["","Compact","Full Size"],[["Weight, grill only","About 14 lb","About 27.6 lb"],["With 1 / 2 griddles","16.2 / 18.4 lb","31.8 / 36.4 lb"],["Packed","About 1&quot; thick","About 1.25&quot; thick"],["Footprint","17.5&quot; × 10.25&quot;","21.75&quot; × 12.75&quot;"],["Cooking area","16.25&quot; × 9&quot; (146 sq in)","20.5&quot; × 11.25&quot; (231 sq in)"],["Height","10.5&quot;","13&quot;"],["Steel","12-gauge carbon steel","10-gauge carbon steel"],["Air gap","2⅞&quot;","3⅝&quot;"],["Price, grill only","$89.97","$149.97"]])}
<h2>By trip type</h2>{table(["Trip","Pick"],[["Kayak, canoe, short walk-in","Compact"],["Car trunk, couple or small family","Compact"],["Tailgate for a crowd","Full Size"],["RV, truck, UTV, boat (as cargo)","Either"],["Backyard patio, family dinners","Full Size"]])}
<p>Slot Grill says the Compact is sized for one to three people; the Full Size suits a family or group and cast iron. Both take one or two <a href="{GRID}">griddle plates</a>.</p>
""","about",[])
page("about","About Portable Slot Grill","Who publishes Portable Slot Grill, what it covers, and where product facts come from.","c13",f"""
<p>Portable Slot Grill is a set of practical guides for charcoal grilling away from home and for small spaces at home.</p>
<h2>Who publishes it</h2><p>Slot Grill. The <a href="{HOME}">Slot Grill</a> is a collapsible carbon steel charcoal grill made in the USA by Keith in Buna, Texas, in a Compact and a Full Size, with an optional griddle.</p>
<h2>How we handle facts</h2>{ul(["Specs and prices come from SlotGrill.com, which is the authority.","Food temperatures follow USDA minimums.","No invented reviews, ratings or testimonials."])}
<p>Questions: use the <a href="{CONTACT}">Slot Grill contact form</a>.</p>
""","about")
page("faq","Portable Grilling FAQ","Answers about portable charcoal grilling: where it's allowed, packing, safety, food and the Slot Grill.","c07","<p>All the questions from across the site, grouped by topic.</p>","about",[("Where can I buy a Slot Grill?","Slot Grill sells direct at SlotGrill.com, the @SlotGrill TikTok Shop and @SlotGrill on the Shop app, and says it has no authorized third-party resellers."),("Is the Slot Grill made in the USA?","Yes. Slot Grill says its grills are made by Keith in Buna, Texas, with U.S.-based partners helping during very high demand.")])
page("glossary","Portable Grilling Glossary","Plain definitions of portable charcoal grilling terms: air gap, chimney starter, flat-pack, two-zone, griddle and more.","c13","<dl>"+"".join("<dt><b>%s</b></dt><dd>%s</dd>"%t for t in [
("Air gap","On the Slot Grill, the space between the table and the bottom of the coal bed: 2⅞&quot; Compact, 3⅝&quot; Full Size."),("Chimney starter","A metal tube for lighting charcoal with paper."),("Flat-pack","A grill that comes apart into flat plates for carrying."),("Two-zone fire","Coals on one side, none on the other."),("Griddle (plancha)","A flat steel cooking plate."),("Grate key","Slot Grill's grate-lifting tool; doubles as a bottle opener."),("Carbon steel","Strong steel that takes seasoning and rusts if left bare and wet."),("Seasoning","Oil baked onto steel as a protective coating."),("Lump charcoal","Charred hardwood; lights fast and hot."),("Briquettes","Pressed charcoal; steady and long."),("Leave No Trace","Outdoor ethic: pack out everything, leave the site as found."),("Tab and slot","How the Slot Grill's panels lock together by hand.")])+"</dl>","about")
